From 20518f2bf30e366ad3de576b5b7ce4105db83c48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: poterya <skvorec.9142@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 20:31:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ArduCopter: add NN_DETECT (mode 29) flight mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a custom flight mode for in-air propeller fault detection. The
vehicle holds horizontal position (Loiter-style) and altitude (Alt-Hold
style) while ignoring all pilot stick input, so the airframe stays
locked to its initial point — important for clean accelerometer-based
vibration analysis.

The detector itself is gated behind a hover-stability check: armed,
in-air, EKF |vxy| <= 0.30 m/s and |vz| <= 0.30 m/s held continuously
for 3 s. Only then it starts feeding the IMU rolling window of 50
body-frame accel samples, computing a de-meaned RMS metric and calling
vibration_fault() — the integration hook for the sklearn-trained
RandomForest / DecisionTree model. Disarm or landing returns the
detector to the waiting state and flushes the buffer.

Status is reported via STATUSTEXT once a second (waiting / ok / BROKEN)
with a one-shot CRITICAL message latched on the first fault transition.

Mode number 29 (gap between TURTLE=28 and the reserved offboard=30),
short name NNDT. Feature can be disabled at compile time by setting
MODE_NN_DETECT_ENABLED to 0.

Files:
  ArduCopter/config.h           - feature flag
  ArduCopter/mode.h             - enum entry + ModeNNDetect class
  ArduCopter/Copter.h           - friend + instance under feature flag
  ArduCopter/mode.cpp           - factory case in mode_from_mode_num
  ArduCopter/mode_nn_detect.cpp - implementation (new file)
---
